.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_KDF-TLS13_KDF 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_KDF-TLS13_KDF
.Nd The TLS 1.3 EVP_KDF implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing the TLS 1.3 version of the
.Sy HKDF
KDF through the
.Sy EVP_KDF
API.
.Pp
The EVP_KDF-TLS13_KDF algorithm implements the HKDF key derivation
function as used by TLS 1.3.
.Pp
The output is considered to be keying material.
.Ss Identity
"TLS13-KDF" is the name for this implementation; it can be used with the
.Xr EVP_KDF_fetch 3
function.
.Ss Supported parameters
The supported parameters are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqdigest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqkey" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
.It \(dqsalt" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SALT Ns ) <octet string>
These parameters work as described in
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 .
.It \(dqprefix" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PREFIX Ns ) <octet string>
This parameter sets the label prefix on the specified TLS 1.3 KDF
context.
For TLS 1.3 this should be set to the ASCII string "tls13 " without a
trailing zero byte.
Refer to RFC 8446 section 7.1 "Key Schedule" for details.
.It \(dqlabel" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_LABEL Ns ) <octet string>
This parameter sets the label on the specified TLS 1.3 KDF context.
Refer to RFC 8446 section 7.1 "Key Schedule" for details.
.It \(dqdata" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_DATA Ns ) <octet string>
This parameter sets the context data on the specified TLS 1.3 KDF
context.
Refer to RFC 8446 section 7.1 "Key Schedule" for details.
.It \(dqmode" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_MODE Ns ) <UTF8 string> or <integer>
This parameter sets the mode for the TLS 1.3 KDF operation.
There are two modes that are currently defined:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqEXTRACT_ONLY" or Sy EVP_KDF_HKDF_MODE_EXTRACT_ONLY
In this mode calling
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3
will just perform the extract operation.
The value returned will be the intermediate fixed-length pseudorandom
key K. The
.Em keylen
parameter must match the size of K, which can be looked up by calling
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_get_kdf_size 3
after setting the mode and digest.
.Pp
The digest, key and salt values must be set before a key is derived
otherwise an error will occur.
.It \(dqEXPAND_ONLY" or Sy EVP_KDF_HKDF_MODE_EXPAND_ONLY
In this mode calling
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3
will just perform the expand operation.
The input key should be set to the intermediate fixed-length
pseudorandom key K returned from a previous extract operation.
.Pp
The digest, key and info values must be set before a key is derived
otherwise an error will occur.
.El
.El
.Pp
The OpenSSL FIPS provider also supports the following parameters:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqfips-indicator" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_FIPS_APPROVED_INDICATOR Ns ) <integer>
A getter that returns 1 if the operation is FIPS approved, or 0
otherwise.
This may be used after calling EVP_KDF_derive.
It returns 0 if any "***-check" related parameter is set to 0 and the
check fails.
.It \(dqdigest-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_FIPS_DIGEST_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
The default value of 1 causes an error during
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3
if used digest is not approved.
Setting this to zero will ignore the error and set the approved
"fips-indicator" to 0. This option breaks FIPS compliance if it causes
the approved "fips-indicator" to return 0.
.Pp
According to RFC 8446, the following are approved digest algorithms:
SHA2-256, SHA2-384.
.It \(dqkey-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_FIPS_KEY_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
The default value of 1 causes an error during
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3
if the length of used key-derivation key
.Pf ( Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY )
is shorter than 112 bits.
Setting this to zero will ignore the error and set the approved
"fips-indicator" to 0. This option breaks FIPS compliance if it causes
the approved "fips-indicator" to return 0.
.El
.Sh NOTES
This KDF is intended for use by the TLS 1.3 implementation in libssl.
It does not support all the options and capabilities that HKDF does.
.Pp
The
.Em OSSL_PARAM
array passed to
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3
or
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3
must specify all of the parameters required.
This KDF does not support a piecemeal approach to providing these.
.Pp
A context for a TLS 1.3 KDF can be obtained by calling:
.Bd -literal
 EVP_KDF *kdf = EVP_KDF_fetch(NULL, "TLS13-KDF", NULL);
 EVP_KDF_CTX *kctx = EVP_KDF_CTX_new(kdf);
.Ed
.Pp
The output length of a TLS 1.3 KDF expand operation is specified via the
.Em keylen
parameter to the
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3
function.
When using EVP_KDF_HKDF_MODE_EXTRACT_ONLY the
.Em keylen
parameter must equal the size of the intermediate fixed-length
pseudorandom key otherwise an error will occur.
For that mode, the fixed output size can be looked up by calling
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_get_kdf_size 3
after setting the mode and digest on the
.Sy EVP_KDF_CTX .
.Sh CONFORMING TO
RFC 8446
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_new 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_free 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_get_kdf_size 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF-HKDF 7
